{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The policy’s high-risk edge is individual-name matching: broad fuzzy matching would catch transliterations but also fail the explicit look-alike limits. I’m using role-aware normalization instead—separate given/family names, discard only permitted patronymic/nasab elements, and encode known transliteration systems—while keeping entities and vessels exact after their allowed designators are removed."}}
